46	      "id": "product-wiki",
47	      "version": "60922.3",
48	      "answers": {
49	        "product": "Fringe Discover: a spontaneity/reachability tool for the Edinburgh Festival Fringe. Where listings apps answer 'what exists?', this answers 'what can I actually make right now?' — given the user's location, how far they'll travel and how, and their next commitment, it collapses ~3,800 shows into a short list of genuinely reachable options that haven't started and still leave time to reach whatever is next.",
50	        "users": "Fringe-goers mid-festival, usually on foot and without a fixed plan — visitors with a gap between a booked show and dinner, locals and tourists intimidated by the programme's scale. Decisive in the moment rather than researchers: they want a short list of good, reachable options, not 3,800 search results. Emotional target: 'delight + relief'.",
51	        "market": "Edinburgh Fringe discovery and planning tools. Alternatives: the official Fringe app (a 'Nearby now' + shake-to-search finder), Plan My Fringe (a schedule optimiser with a walking-time 'Fringe Trail'), the edfringe.com programme and filters, the Half Price Hut (same-day discounts), review outlets such as ThreeWeeks, plus street posters and word-of-mouth. None centres full reachability — travel mode plus next-commitment slack — the way Fringe Discover does."
52	      }
