81	      "reason": "the executable-requirements layout is a framework contract: cases live in <kind>/cases/ and the harness in shared/, so every case's reach to shared/ and to the shipped modules under js/, plan/ and shared/ is fixed by the pack's layout standard, not a placement choice"
82	    },
83	    {
84	      "rule": "claudinite-isolation",
85	      "path": "scripts/verify.sh",
86	      "reason": "the repo's one verification gate invokes the world sweep (engine/checks/check_the_world.mjs) so that passing it locally means what passing CI means — a commit that passed verify and went red on CI for a blocking conformance finding is what prompted this. Not the coupling the rule guards against: no canon internals are imported and nothing is inlined, it is the same documented CLI entry point .github/workflows/ already spells under the rule's own carve-out. A canon rename of that one path breaks the workflow and this script identically, and the fix is the same one line"
87	    }
